<title>TURKEY: Turkish cb reserve falls to $16.5 bln at end-1996.</title>
<headline>Turkish cb reserve falls to $16.5 bln at end-1996.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Friday its foreign currency reserve fell to $16.491 billion in the last week of 1996 ending on December 27, down $762 million from a week ago.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollar</p>
<p>		   December 27   December 20   end-1995</p>
<p> Forex reserve   16.491	  17.253	 12.391</p>
<p> Gold reserve     1.383	   1.383	  1.383</p>
<p> Total reserve   17.874	  18.636	 13.774</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, rose by $325 million to an all-time high of $28.834 billion in the week ending December 13, the bank said.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
